        <title type="html"><![CDATA[ci(workflows): specify `pull_request_target` branches]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41741</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41741"/>
        <updated>2025-10-29T17:30:56.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Update all workflows using <code class="notranslate">pull_request_target</code> to specify trusted target branches, such as <code class="notranslate">main</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Security best practice to limit <code class="notranslate">pull_request_target</code> workflows to trusted branches, reducing the attack surface for malicious pull requests.</p>
<p dir="auto">The <code class="notranslate">pull_request_target</code> trigger causes the workflow to run in the context of the base branch with access to secrets, so it's important:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>to specify <strong>only</strong> trusted branches, to avoid that the workflow runs on an untrusted branch,</li>
<li>to specify <strong>all</strong> trusted branches, to avoid that the workflow is skipped on PRs targeting a trusted branch.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">See: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-workflows/events-that-trigger-workflows#pull_request_target">https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-workflows/events-that-trigger-workflows#pull_request_target</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">Part of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3566969685" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1021" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/fred/issues/1021/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1021">mdn/fred#1021</a>.</p>]]></content>
