        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Technical review: Add doc covering bounce tracking mitigations]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41740</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41740"/>
        <updated>2025-10-29T16:37:31.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://privacysandbox.google.com/protections/bounce-tracking-mitigations" rel="nofollow">Bounce tracking mitigations</a> is a privacy-protecting feature available from Chromium 116 onwards, which also has support in Firefox and Safari in similar forms. It is <a href="https://privacycg.github.io/nav-tracking-mitigations/#bounce-tracking-mitigations" rel="nofollow">specified here</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a page explaining how it works. This is one of the privacy sandbox features that is fully released and being kept, which I hadn't gotten around to documenting.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that is is a browser feature, and not a web platform feature. As a result, it doesn't really have a sensible way to record it in BCD.</p>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

