        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Document ARIA attributes for SVG element]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41736</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41736"/>
        <updated>2025-10-29T15:54:02.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144060585?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">Documents that various ARIA-attributes are valid for the <code class="notranslate">&lt;svg&gt;</code> element.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">It is not clear on this page if the <code class="notranslate">&lt;svg&gt;</code> element supports any other attributes than the ones listed. Most other pages have something along the lines of:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">This element's attributes include the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes" rel="nofollow">global attributes</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">(see e.g. <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/button#attributes" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">&lt;button&gt;</code></a>,  <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/div#attributes" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">&lt;div&gt;</code></a>)</p>
<p dir="auto">I saw some examples on MDN (e.g. on the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Reference/Attributes/aria-label" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">aria-label</code> page</a>) use ARIA labels on the <code class="notranslate">&lt;svg&gt;</code> element, but it's not clear on this page if this is supported or not. I had to go into the specification to find out.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<p dir="auto">The ARIA-attributes are listed as supported in the <a href="https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/struct.html#SVGElement" rel="nofollow">specification</a>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>




<p dir="auto">None</p>]]></content>
